            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the French for (film) director, then the French for shooting."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: zapper",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zapper — \"to channel-hop; to skip\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Le soir, il zappe d'une chaîne à l'autre. In the evening he flicks from one channel to another."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Informally, to forget or skip: j'ai zappé le rendez-vous."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zapper was borrowed from English zap (EtymDB), an imitative word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
